                         Patch Metadata - Gen 3/50 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                          
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_crx_mixed                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters and choices in the current approach:                                       │
│                          │ - N_UPLOADS=3, N_REPEATS=2 fixed; feature map is RX(2π/3 * cell_value).                   │
│                          │ - The ANSATZ block structure, number of parameters per block, and entangling pattern      │
│                          │ strongly determine expressivity and generalization.                                       │
│                          │ - The existing block used heavy parameter sharing (good for regularization) but limited   │
│                          │ parametric two-qubit rotations (CRZ only), and either many or few local phases depending  │
│                          │ on the seed.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ What I changed and why it should improve performance:                                     │
│                          │ - Introduced symmetry-aware parameter grouping that breaks perfect rotational symmetry in │
│                          │ a controlled way (splitting corner and edge groups into two subgroups). This keeps        │
│                          │ parameter efficiency while giving the circuit freedom to distinguish different board      │
│                          │ orientations.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Replaced purely-phase controlled entanglers with parametrized CRX entanglers on the     │
│                          │ ring and hub edges, giving tunable entangling rotations (stronger mixing than CRZ-only).  │
│                          │ Two entangler params (crx_ring, crx_hub) balance expressivity and regularization.         │
│                          │ - Added light local pre/post-phase layers shared by symmetry classes (rz_corner, rz_edge, │
│                          │ rz_center, rz_out) and local RX adjustments to increase local feature mixing.             │
│                          │ - Added a compact final mixing layer (shared ry_out + rz_out) to aggregate information    │
│                          │ before measurement.                                                                       │
│                          │ - Kept parameter sharing deliberate to limit total parameters per block to 15 (leading to │
│                          │ 90 total parameters for the full circuit), slightly increasing expressivity over the      │
│                          │ 84-parameter variant while remaining parameter-efficient.                                 │
│                          │ - Included a few fixed CZ edges could optionally be used to increase entanglement without │
│                          │ adding parameters; here I rely on CRX for parametric entanglement and keep fixed gates    │
│                          │ minimal to control depth.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome:                                                                         │
│                          │ - More expressive two-qubit parametric entangling (CRX) and structured local rotations    │
│                          │ should improve test/validation accuracy and lower L2 loss.                                │
│                          │ - Controlled parameter-sharing maintains good generalization and parameter efficiency.    │
