│ patch_description        │ Reduce gate count and parameter count while preserving expressive, symmetry-aware         │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
│                          │ I replace the previous heavy per-block layout (many single-qubit layers and 12            │
│                          │ parameterized CRX edges) with a compact, symmetry-grouped single-qubit layer (shared RY   │
│                          │ and RZ by corner/edge/center classes) plus a partial entangling layer of CZs (selecting 4 │
│                          │ ring edges and 4 hub edges). This halves the entangling operations per block and          │
│                          │ collapses many per-wire parameters into 6 shared parameters per block, improving          │
│                          │ parameter efficiency, reducing depth/gate-count, and adding regularization via weight     │
│                          │ sharing. The smaller parameter set should train faster with Adam and generalize better    │
│                          │ while keeping enough entanglement to model board structure.                               │
