│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_symmetry_split_mixing                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce tunable parametrized entangling (CRZ) layers targeted to Z-basis readout, and   │
│                          │ expand per-class symmetry-aware single-qubit rotations with light symmetry-breaking       │
│                          │ between corner/edge pairs. Add compact final RY+RZ output adjustments that include        │
│                          │ separate periphery vs center parameters so the ansatz can align rotations with the        │
│                          │ Z-observables used for classification. Parameter sharing keeps the block compact while    │
│                          │ giving the circuit more expressive entangling and Z-phase control (CRZ) which should      │
│                          │ improve mapping to the measured Z expectations and help both accuracy and generalization. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Split corners and edges into two symmetry-related pairs to allow controlled asymmetry   │
│                          │ without exploding parameters.                                                             │
│                          │ - Replace fixed CZ entanglers with parametrized CRZ on ring and hub edges (shared         │
│                          │ per-class) so the entanglement strength (phase) is trainable and directly affects         │
│                          │ Z-expectations.                                                                           │
│                          │ - Keep class-based sharing for single-qubit phases to regularize and keep parameters      │
│                          │ efficient.                                                                                │
│                          │ - Add final shared RY and RZ periphery/center adjustments to better shape outputs in the  │
│                          │ Z-basis.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity and parameter efficiency (moderate increase in N_PARAMS) and   │
│                          │ respects grid adjacency and allowed gate sets.                                            │
