│ patch_name               │ shared_crx_cry_symmetry_compact                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ I propose a compact, symmetry-aware ansatz that (1) reduces the number of independent     │
│                          │ parameters via deliberate sharing across corner/edge/center symmetry classes, (2)         │
│                          │ replaces purely Z-controlled entanglers with a mix of CRY on the ring and CRX on hub      │
│                          │ edges to better convert the RX-encoded features into Z-readout space, and (3) retains     │
│                          │ light single-qubit mixing before measurement. This yields fewer unique parameters (better │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and regularization) while adding cross-qubit X/Y mixing that helps   │
│                          │ map the RX feature-map information into measurable Z expectations. All two-qubit gates    │
│                          │ remain on allowed adjacent grid edges and only allowed gates are used.                    │
