│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_rz_output_layer                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.46 with good test accuracy (0.53) but  │
│                          │ suffers from a large generalization gap (0.12) and moderate validation accuracy (0.47).   │
│                          │ The prior programs show that adding a lightweight final RZ layer after the RY output      │
│                          │ layer can sharpen phase boundaries in the readout basis without significantly increasing  │
│                          │ parameter count.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests augmenting the final single-qubit layer with shared RZ        │
│                          │ rotations immediately after the existing RY_out layer. This follows the pattern of        │
│                          │ symmetry-aware parameter sharing already proven effective in the current design:          │
│                          │ - rz_out_corner: shared across corners (0, 2, 4, 6)                                       │
│                          │ - rz_out_edge: shared across edges (1, 3, 5, 7)                                           │
│                          │ - rz_out_center: dedicated to center (8)                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This adds only 3 parameters per block (9 total across all blocks) while providing         │
│                          │ fine-grained phase control that can help:                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Reduce the train-test generalization gap by improving decision boundary sharpness      │
│                          │ 2. Improve validation accuracy through better phase alignment                             │
│                          │ 3. Maintain parameter efficiency since we're adding minimal overhead                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The RZ gates work synergistically with the RY output gates: RY rotates in the XY plane    │
│                          │ while RZ applies phase shifts, allowing the model to carve more precise decision surfaces │
│                          │ in the measurement basis.                                                                 │
