│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ refine_corners_reduce_entanglement                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Refine symmetry and reduce unnecessary entangling to improve generalization and           │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Keep the useful diagonal corner symmetry by splitting corners into two diagonal         │
│                          │ subclasses: (0,4) and (2,6). This matches the suggested motif to better capture diagonal  │
│                          │ win patterns.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Merge edge rotations back into a single shared edge parameter (less fragmentation than  │
│                          │ prior split) to reduce parameters and regularize.                                         │
│                          │ - Replace the expensive full parametrized ring CRX layer with a sparser fixed-CZ ring (4  │
│                          │ symmetric ring edges) to lower depth and gate count, while keeping a small number of      │
│                          │ parametrized hub CRX gates to preserve tunable centre–edge coupling.                      │
│                          │ - Remove the redundant per-wire RX layer and instead add a compact shared RX mixing       │
│                          │ (periphery vs center) to keep expressivity with far fewer parameters.                     │
│                          │ - Use a small shared output layer (periphery vs center) for sharper decisions.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected effect:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Fewer unique parameters per block (parameter efficiency improved).                      │
│                          │ - Lower circuit depth and gate count (faster training and less overfitting).              │
│                          │ - Retains expressivity for diagonal patterns and center coupling via the hub CRX.         │
