│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ periphery_center_sharing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce parameter count and circuit depth to improve generalization and parameter          │
│                          │ efficiency by reverting aggressive diagonal splitting and adopting a compact              │
│                          │ periphery-vs-center sharing motif. This block:                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Shares rotations across all peripheral cells (corners/edges) and the center, cutting    │
│                          │ unique parameters from 16+ down to 9 per block (N_PARAMS drops from 96 to 54).            │
│                          │ - Keeps a small symmetric RZ phase (periphery vs center) to break parity while staying    │
│                          │ compact.                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Uses a reduced entangling pattern (6 CZs) to lower depth and gate count but retains     │
│                          │ connectivity to the center for mixing.                                                    │
│                          │ - Adds a shared RX mixing across periphery and center plus a small final RY output layer  │
│                          │ (periphery vs center) to sharpen decision boundaries.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes should reduce overfitting (smaller generalization gap), improve parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency, and often raise test accuracy by focusing capacity and lowering depth.        │
