│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_entangling_and_mid_block_rz                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate used CRZ gates for all entanglers, which may have limited the      │
│                          │ generation of entanglement compared to fixed CZ gates. This edit introduces a hybrid      │
│                          │ entangling layer: it uses fixed CZ gates for the ring (periphery) to ensure strong        │
│                          │ entanglement, while retaining parametrized CRZ gates for the hub (center) to allow the    │
│                          │ model to learn how to weight the center qubit's influence.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, following the recommendation to break residual parity patterns, I've added  │
│                          │ a mid-block RZ layer. This layer uses shared parameters for the periphery and center,     │
│                          │ providing a lightweight phase adjustment after entanglement but before the RX mixing      │
│                          │ layer. This should improve the expressivity of the feature transformations within each    │
│                          │ repetition.                                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0153                                                                                   │
