│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diagonal_symmetry_split                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.44) has degraded from the baseline (score 0.51) despite      │
│                          │ adding parametrized entangling gates (CRY, CRX). The issue appears to be:                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Over-parameterization**: The current ANSATZ_SPEC has 72 parameters (vs. 54 in the    │
│                          │ baseline), which increases optimization difficulty without clear benefit. The             │
│                          │ parametrized controlled rotations add complexity but the model struggles to learn         │
│                          │ effectively.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Loss of symmetry structure**: The baseline's simple RZ pre-phases (shared periphery  │
│                          │ vs. center) worked well. The current version splits RZ into corner/edge/center, adding    │
│                          │ parameters without improving expressivity.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Entanglement pattern mismatch**: The CRY on all 8 ring edges plus CRX on 4 hub edges │
│                          │ creates a dense, high-depth circuit (depth 76 vs. 40 baseline) that may suffer from       │
│                          │ barren plateaus and gradient issues.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed fix**: Implement the "diagonal symmetry split" recommendation from the problem │
│                          │ statement. Replace the uniform corner/edge RZ sharing with two diagonal classes:          │
│                          │ - **Main-diagonal corners** (qubits 0 & 4): share `rz_diag_main`                          │
│                          │ - **Anti-diagonal corners** (qubits 2 & 6): share `rz_diag_anti`                          │
│                          │ - **Edges** (qubits 1, 3, 5, 7): keep shared `rz_edge`                                    │
│                          │ - **Center** (qubit 8): keep `rz_center`                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This adds only 2 parameters per block (58 total vs. 54 baseline) while capturing diagonal │
│                          │ win-line structure. Simultaneously, **revert the parametrized entangling gates to fixed   │
│                          │ CZ gates** (like the baseline) to reduce depth and avoid barren plateaus. The fixed CZ    │
│                          │ pattern is simpler and the added RZ parameters provide enough expressivity.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances parameter efficiency with structural awareness of the tic-tac-toe grid's    │
│                          │ diagonal symmetries.                                                                      │
