│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared-compact-entangler-with-parameter-efficiency                                        │
│ patch_description        │ I propose a compact, symmetry-aware ansatz that reduces parameter count and circuit depth │
│                          │ while keeping expressive entanglement around the central hub. Key ideas:                  │
│                          │ - Aggressively share parameters across the periphery (all eight outer cells) to encode    │
│                          │ rotational symmetry and improve generalization.                                           │
│                          │ - Keep a distinct center parameter to allow the hub to behave differently.                │
│                          │ - Replace multiple fixed hub-CZs with parameterized CRZ gates sharing a single "ent"      │
│                          │ parameter so entanglement strength is trainable but parameter-efficient.                  │
│                          │ - Keep a small RX mixing layer and a final RY+RZ sharpening layer, both using shared      │
│                          │ periphery/center parameters to reduce parameter dimensionality.                           │
│                          │ This reduces N_PARAMS (faster training, less overfitting), lowers depth and gate count,   │
│                          │ and adds a single learnable entangling strength to tune center-periphery coupling — a     │
│                          │ useful inductive bias for the tic-tac-toe geometry.                                       │
