╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_crx_efficient_ansatz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This proposal replaces the ansatz block with a symmetry-aware, parameter-efficient design │
│                          │ that combines shared single-qubit rotations with compact parametrized controlled          │
│                          │ rotations (CRX) for entanglement. Key design choices:                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency: only 9 unique parameters per block (shared across wires/gates),   │
│                          │ giving N_PARAMS = 9 * N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS = 54. This matches the best prior compact     │
│                          │ configuration while improving expressivity.                                               │
│                          │ - Symmetry-aware sharing: corners, edges, and center use their own shared rotation        │
│                          │ parameters (ry_corner, ry_edge, ry_center). This encodes the grid symmetries and reduces  │
│                          │ redundant degrees of freedom.                                                             │
│                          │ - CRX entanglement: use parametrized controlled-X rotations for both ring edges           │
│                          │ (crx_ring) and hub edges to center (crx_hub). Parametrized two-qubit gates increase       │
│                          │ entangling expressivity per parameter compared to fixed CZ gates.                         │
│                          │ - Small phase layer (rz_periphery / rz_center) and final RX mixing (rx_periphery /        │
│                          │ rx_center) provide additional controllable interference and mixing without blowing up     │
│                          │ parameter count.                                                                          │
│                          │ - All two-qubit gates respect the allowed adjacency set.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected benefits: improved expressivity per parameter (via CRX), better generalization   │
│                          │ through symmetry-driven parameter sharing, and low parameter count and depth for more     │
│                          │ reliable optimization with Adam. The interface, inputs, and outputs remain unchanged.     │
