│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rx_and_reduce_entangling_depth                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Refine the ansatz to improve generalization and reduce circuit depth. Changes:            │
│                          │ - Replace parametrized CRX-heavy entangling (which drove up depth and gate count) with a  │
│                          │ compact fixed CZ entangling pattern (symmetric reduced ring + two hub links). This lowers │
│                          │ depth and regularizes the model.                                                          │
│                          │ - Split the shared RX mixing parameter into rx_corner and rx_edge (keeping rx_center) so  │
│                          │ corners and edges can be mixed differently while keeping parameter growth minimal (one    │
│                          │ extra RX param).                                                                          │
│                          │ - Add a small final RY output layer (shared periphery vs center) to sharpen readout       │
│                          │ decision boundaries without a large parameter increase.                                   │
