│ patch_name               │ parametrized_entangling_with_shared_angles                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace several fixed CZ entanglers with parameterized controlled-rotations that reuse    │
│                          │ existing shared angle keys.                                                               │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Parametrized two-qubit gates (CRX/CRZ) let the optimizer tune entangling strength       │
│                          │ rather than relying on fixed maximal-phase CZs,                                           │
│                          │   improving trainability and expressivity.                                                │
│                          │ - Reusing existing shared parameters (rx_periphery, rz_center) keeps the per-block        │
│                          │ parameter count unchanged (parameter efficiency preserved)                                │
│                          │   while injecting nontrivial controllable correlations between ring/periphery qubits and  │
│                          │ the center hub.                                                                           │
│                          │ - The new pattern respects adjacency constraints and symmetry (alternating ring CRX edges │
│                          │ and hub CRZ spokes), keeping the architecture compact.                                    │
│                          │ This edit only modifies the ANSATZ_SPEC inside the allowed EVOLVE block.                  │
