│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ symm_crx_entangler                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate ansatz is a crossover combining the compact symmetry-aware single-qubit    │
│                          │ sharing from one parent with the parametrized controlled-rotation entangling motif from   │
│                          │ the other. The ansatz:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Groups single-qubit rotations by board symmetry (corners, edges, center) to reduce      │
│                          │ parameters and regularize learning.                                                       │
│                          │ - Adds a small RZ periphery vs center phase to break parity symmetry.                     │
│                          │ - Uses parametrized CRX on ring edges and CRZ on spokes to the hub, reusing a single      │
│                          │ entangling RX parameter for both CRX entanglement and RX mixing to keep parameter count   │
│                          │ low while boosting tunable entanglement.                                                  │
│                          │ - Ends with a compact shared RY output layer (periphery vs center) for sharper class      │
│                          │ boundaries.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Design goals:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Keep N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK small and consistent (9 keys) so training budget and optimizer  │
│                          │ settings remain aligned with the fixed training loop.                                     │
│                          │ - Use parameter sharing to improve parameter efficiency and regularize the model.         │
│                          │ - Favor CRX/CRZ entangling (richer than only CZ) to improve expressivity without          │
│                          │ inflating the parameter count.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This program preserves the original inputs/outputs and training loop while replacing only │
│                          │ the ANSATZ_SPEC inside the EVOLVE block.                                                  │
