╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parametrized_shared_entanglers_54params                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed CZ entanglers and larger per-qubit RX/RZ parametrization with a         │
│                          │ compact, symmetry-aware block that uses parametrized controlled rotations (CRX on ring    │
│                          │ edges, CRZ on spokes) and aggressive parameter sharing across symmetric wires.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Trainable two-qubit gates (CRX/CRZ) increase expressivity versus fixed CZs while        │
│                          │ keeping depth similar.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Sharing parameters by symmetry (corners/edges/center, periphery vs center, ring vs      │
│                          │ spoke entanglers) keeps the parameter count down to 9 per block, yielding N_PARAMS = 9 *  │
│                          │ (N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS) = 54 total. This matches the better-performing prior seed and     │
│                          │ improves parameter efficiency.                                                            │
│                          │ - The design preserves adjacency constraints and keeps entangler count modest (4 ring + 4 │
│                          │ spokes) for reasonable depth/gate_count.                                                  │
│                          │ - Using a single small shared RZ across wires for parity-breaking reduces parameters      │
│                          │ while maintaining a global phase bias.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change should increase expressivity with efficient parameter usage and favor better  │
│                          │ train/test performance and lower generalization gap.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0139                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
