│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ periphery_center_shared_cr_entangler                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce parameter count while keeping expressivity by grouping qubits into                 │
│                          │ corner/edge/center symmetry buckets and using shared parametrized controlled rotations    │
│                          │ for entangling. This replacement:                                                         │
│                          │ - Collapses many distinct single-qubit parameters into three RY groups (corners, edges,   │
│                          │ center) and two RZ groups (periphery vs center).                                          │
│                          │ - Uses shared CRX on ring edges and shared CRZ on the four spokes to the hub to introduce │
│                          │ tunable two-qubit interactions with only two entangling parameters.                       │
│                          │ - Adds a compact RX mixing layer with periphery vs center sharing.                        │
│                          │ - Reuses the compact single-qubit parameters in the final "sharpen" RY/RZ layers to avoid │
│                          │ increasing unique parameter keys.                                                         │
│                          │ This yields N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK = 9 and total N_PARAMS = 54 (matching the paper's sweet    │
│                          │ spot), reducing overparameterization, encouraging regularization, and keeping             │
│                          │ geometry-aware symmetry that should improve generalization and training efficiency.       │
