│ patch_description        │ Append a small shared RZ "sharpening" layer after the existing per-qubit RY_out layer.    │
│                          │ This adds only two new parameters per ansatz block: "rz_out_periphery" (shared across     │
│                          │ qubits 0–7)                                                                               │
│                          │ and "rz_out_center" (qubit 8). Small end-of-circuit Z phases often improve class          │
│                          │ separability                                                                              │
│                          │ with negligible extra depth and very few additional parameters, breaking residual parity  │
│                          │ symmetries and sharpening decision boundaries. This is a low-cost, symmetry-aware change  │
│                          │ intended to boost validation/test accuracy without dramatically increasing gate count.    │
