│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diagonal_crx_entangler_motif                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a very sparse fixed CZ entangler that lacks sufficient mixing     │
│                          │ between non-adjacent sectors of the board. This proposal introduces a "diagonal"          │
│                          │ entangling motif using CRX gates on pairs (0,3), (2,5), (4,7), and (6,1). These edges are │
│                          │ physically adjacent on the 3x3 grid (corners to adjacent edges) and provide a stronger    │
│                          │ mixing pathway between the quadrants of the board.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By sharing a single parameter `ent_rx` across these four CRX gates, we increase the       │
│                          │ expressive power of the circuit with minimal parameter overhead. This helps the model     │
│                          │ capture the diagonal and cross-sector correlations essential for identifying winning      │
│                          │ lines in tic-tac-toe, while maintaining a depth that fits within the successful 40–52     │
│                          │ range.                                                                                    │
