╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_init_rz_and_param_hub_crz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a small initial Z-phase layer (shared periphery vs center) before the first RY  │
│                          │ rotations to break early parity symmetries and help optimization, and make the center     │
│                          │ coupling tunable by replacing two fixed hub CZs with a shared CRZ parameter ("crz_hub").  │
│                          │ This is the lightweight recommendation from the notes: tiny initial Z phases are low-cost │
│                          │ but often improve expressivity and training, and a single shared param for the hub links  │
│                          │ allows the model to adapt center-periphery coupling without exploding parameter count.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Add RZ "rz_init_periphery" on qubits 0–7 and "rz_init_center" on qubit 8 at the top of  │
│                          │ the block (applied before RY).                                                            │
│                          │ - Replace CZ on [1,8] and [5,8] with parametrized CRZ gates sharing "crz_hub".            │
│                          │ - Keep the rest of the compact, symmetry-aware sharing motif to remain                    │
│                          │ parameter-efficient.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These modifications keep two-qubit gates on allowed edges, use only supported gates, and  │
│                          │ add only a small number of parameters while aiming to improve validation/generalization.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0118                                                                                   │
