│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_crx_entanglement_and_parameter_refinement                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate used a high-depth entangling layer (depth 76) with low validation  │
│                          │ accuracy (0.42). I am refining the entangling motif to use CRX gates selectively on both  │
│                          │ the ring and hub edges but reducing the depth by grouping independent pairs.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Specifically, I'm replacing the `CRY_ring` with `CRX` gates on the grid edges to better   │
│                          │ match the `RX` feature map encoding. I've also simplified the parameter sharing: instead  │
│                          │ of separating periphery and center for every single layer, I've returned to the           │
│                          │ three-class symmetry (corner, edge, center) for the initial and final layers, which helps │
│                          │ the model distinguish the 8-fold symmetry of the Tic-Tac-Toe board while maintaining      │
│                          │ parameter efficiency.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
