│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_periphery_center                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a single shared parameter `rz_periphery` for all 9 qubits to      │
│                          │ break parity. While parameter-efficient, this forces the center qubit (which is the sole  │
│                          │ contributor to the 'draw' expectation value) to rotate identically to the periphery.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By splitting this into `rz_periphery` (qubits 0-7) and `rz_center` (qubit 8), we allow    │
│                          │ the model to learn a distinct phase for the center cell. This adds only one parameter per │
│                          │ block (6 total across the circuit) but significantly improves the model's ability to      │
│                          │ distinguish between winning states (periphery-heavy) and draws (center-heavy), sharpening │
│                          │ the decision boundaries.                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
