│ patch_name               │ symmetry_compact_crx_cry_block                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This proposal performs a crossover combining the compact, symmetry-aware parameter        │
│                          │ sharing from the better-performing compact designs with a targeted, parameter-efficient   │
│                          │ entangling motif inspired by the more expressive CRX/CRY mixtures. The new ANSATZ_SPEC    │
│                          │ keeps the number of unique parameters per block low (9), which yields N_PARAMS = 9 *      │
│                          │ N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS = 54 — matching the successful compact candidate — while adding     │
│                          │ sparse parametrized two-qubit rotations: CRY on a reduced set of ring edges (four         │
│                          │ alternating ring links) and CRX on the four spokes to the hub. This trades off some       │
│                          │ entangling density for lower depth and gate count while preserving axis-mixing            │
│                          │ complementary to the RX feature map. Single-qubit layers are symmetry-shared between      │
│                          │ corners, edges, and center to capture board structure while remaining                     │
│                          │ parameter-efficient. The block order (initial RY, a shared RZ pre-phase, sparse CRY/CRX   │
│                          │ entangling, RX mixing, and a compact final RY) keeps circuits shallow and expressive for  │
│                          │ better generalization with fewer parameters.                                              │
