│ patch_description        │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC applies CZ gates only on ring edges (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), (6,7)    │
│                          │ but does not include any fixed entanglement gates connecting the center qubit to the hub. │
│                          │ Meanwhile, parametrized CRX gates connect (1,8), (3,8), (5,8), (7,8).                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By adding fixed CZ gates on (3,8) and (7,8), we fully connect the center qubit to all     │
│                          │ four cardinal hub edges with fixed (parameter-free) two-qubit gates. This enriches the    │
│                          │ entangling landscape and improves information flow through the center without increasing  │
│                          │ the parameter count.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added depth is minimal (~2 gates per block, ~6 gates total over 3 uploads × 2         │
│                          │ repeats), keeping the circuit in the efficient regime. This aligns with the system's      │
│                          │ recommendation to "fully connect the center qubit by appending CZ gates on (3, 8) and (7, │
│                          │ 8)."                                                                                      │
